From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:21:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 145/342] meson_gpio: claims and ioctls for programs, PWM on
 pins 11 and 19

Programs get a binary interface (headers/private/drivers/meson_gpio.h):
an open file claims header pins (one owner at a time, the text commands
leave them alone; their state is saved for "release"), sets them as
inputs or outputs, reads and writes them all at once, and makes pins 11
and 19 PWM outputs. Closing makes its GPIO pins inputs; PWM outputs stay.
"gpio <pin> pwm <0-255>" does the same from the shell.

PWM: the EF controller (E on pin 11, F on 19) counting the crystal, 255
cycles a period (94.1 kHz); 0 and 255 hold the pin low or high, which the
controller can't. Pin 33's PWM A is left out: its controller's B channel
sets one of the ODROID-C2's core voltage regulators. Pins 3 and 5 (I2C A,
the RTC shield) aren't offered any more. Facts: the port's
docs/m27-geekport-facts.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
